1
00:00:00,318 --> 00:00:05,150
FreshBench: does your AI agent know the world has changed?

2
00:00:05,150 --> 00:00:10,159
AI agents confidently repeat facts that USED to be true: old champions, former CEOs, outdated versions.

3
00:00:10,159 --> 00:00:14,483
And most benchmarks freeze their answers, so they go stale too.

4
00:00:14,483 --> 00:00:19,488
FreshBench: every LLM call (agents and judge) goes through the Bifrost gateway.

5
00:00:19,488 --> 00:00:25,494
Bifrost gives one API for all providers, virtual-key governance, automatic fallbacks, and latency/token/cost telemetry.

6
00:00:25,494 --> 00:00:34,676
Every time-sensitive claim is checked against the live web with Tavily. No frozen gold answers.

7
00:00:34,676 --> 00:00:39,682
The dashboard. This demo runs in offline SIMULATION mode with a fictional world (no API keys).

8
00:00:39,682 --> 00:00:45,128
Stale-Answer Detector: paste any AI answer and ask whether it is still true today.

9
00:00:45,128 --> 00:00:48,674
Example: an older model says the CEO of Acme Robotics is Dana Whitfield.

10
00:00:48,674 --> 00:00:53,534
The detector extracts claims, searches Tavily with a neutral query, and judges each claim.

11
00:00:53,534 --> 00:00:58,040
Verdict: STALE. The answer used to be true, but newer evidence supersedes it.

12
00:00:58,040 --> 00:01:03,458
It auto-repairs the answer with the current fact, a source, and an "as of" date.

13
00:01:03,458 --> 00:01:11,267
Each claim shows its Tavily query, confidence, explanation, current truth and evidence links.

14
00:01:11,267 --> 00:01:20,823
Bifrost call trace: claim extraction, verification and repair, each with provider, tokens, latency and cost.

15
00:01:20,823 --> 00:01:25,829
The benchmark: the same models inside 3 agent designs, closed_book, search_rag and guarded.

16
00:01:25,829 --> 00:01:31,754
Closed-book agents go stale. Grounded agents stay fresh. FreshBench measures the cost of freshness.

17
00:01:31,754 --> 00:01:38,635
Leaderboard: fresh rate, stale rate, cost per fresh answer, latency, tokens, Bifrost fallbacks, errors.

18
00:01:38,635 --> 00:01:44,933
Freshness vs cost: top-left is best. Stale rate by topic shows where agents fall behind.

19
00:01:44,933 --> 00:01:53,474
Drill down into any question to compare every agent's answer, cost, latency and the route Bifrost used.

20
00:01:53,474 --> 00:01:58,004
Run new benchmarks from the UI: pick agents, models and a Bifrost fallback chain.

21
00:01:58,004 --> 00:02:03,855
Every agent run is routed through Bifrost and judged by the same fixed Stale-Answer Detector.

22
00:02:03,855 --> 00:02:09,699
Also available as a CLI: check, run, leaderboard, calibrate. Verified end to end against the real Bifrost container.

23
00:02:09,699 --> 00:02:14,706
FreshBench: because "correct" has an expiry date. Code on GitHub.
